<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ashikaga Haruuji</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1508–<a href="/years/1560">1560</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ashikaga Haruuji was the fourth Koga kubo, head of the eastern branch of the Ashikaga in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanto-region">Kantō region</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. At first allied with the Later Hōjō, who helped him destroy his uncle Yoshiaki in 1538, he married a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-ujitsuna">Hōjō Ujitsuna</a>. He later joined the Uesugi against the Hōjō and shared their defeat at Kawagoe in 1546, after which the Hōjō controlled the Koga kubo.</p></div>
